  "title": "Japanese Miso Eggplant",
  "description": "This dish is absolutely gorgeous. Sure, miso paste is salty, but it’s also a little sweet, a little earthy and almost fruity. Combined with the hungry eggplant (which loves to drink up flavour), this is a unique recipe that we think you’ll find yourself making again and again. Chuck some quintessential Japanese coriander and black sesame seeds and you’re away! Pro Tip: Try adding a teaspoon of vinegar and sugar to your cooked rice for that sticky, sushi style hit. Rice wine vinegar is even better!",
